course: dictionary
lesson: 3825
title: Formal and informal words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Formal means serious, polite and following proper rules. You use it in important or official situations, such as writing to a headteacher or meeting a stranger. A formal letter might start with «Dear Sir or Madam», and it uses full words and no slang.
explain: Informal means relaxed and chatty, the way you talk to mates and family. The style you choose for a situation is called your register. Ask yourself: would I say this to my teacher, or only to my best friend?
explain: The word formal also appears in other places. Formal clothes are smart clothes for special events. In maths, a formal method is the written column method, done in the proper way.
fact: Formal means serious and following proper rules, used in important or official situations.
fact: Formal clothes are smart clothes worn for special events.
fact: Formal language is polite and careful, not chatty or slangy.
fact: Formal can also mean official, or done in the proper way.
fact: Everyone has two ways of talking: informal and formal, and the style you choose is your register.
exercise: Which of these is a formal way to start a letter? | Hey you | *Dear Sir or Madam | Hiya mate
exercise: What should you wear to a formal event? | *Smart clothes | Muddy wellies | Pyjamas
exercise: Which sentence uses formal language? | Thanks, see you later, bye! | Oi, what's up? | *I would be grateful if you could reply at your earliest convenience. | Lol, cool.
test: In «batkY means parents, while bAtko is a formal word for father», what does formal tell you about bAtko? | It is a bad word | It is a joke word | It is only for children | *It is the polite, careful word
test: With an adult you have just met, which is the safest way to start? | Hiya | *Mrs Patel | Oi you | Yo
exam: Which sentence would be best in a formal letter to a headteacher? | Hey, can I have a day off, cheers | *I am writing to request a day off school for a family event. | Can I have a day off? Ta | Gonna need the day off, sorry
